{"step_index":2008,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:56:52Z","input_tokens":2570,"cache_read_tokens":51412,"output_tokens":1334,"content":"**Service Identifier (SID).**\n\nIn edge telecommunications (3GPP / PCC / diameter edge routing), a **Service Identifier** is what classifies and directs traffic inside a bearer stream: the edge router inspects the Service Identifier to route, meter, and enforce policy for a specific service without ever needing an application-layer web session.\n\n---\n\n### How the Service Identifier (SID) Works in Our Stack\n\nThis maps directly to our **OP-DBUS subid grammar**:\n```\n<category>.<component-type>.<subject>.<verb>[.<facet>][@vN]\n```\nFor example:\n* `mut.service.escrow.transfer@v1` (The Title & Escrow Service Identifier)\n* `obs.service.valuation.query@v1` (The Acquisition Valuation Service Identifier)\n* `mut.service.cognitive.memory.record@v1` (The Cognitive Memory Service Identifier)\n\n### The Edge Routing Flow\n\n1. **Incoming Request (via Xray)**:\n   A client or edge device connects requesting a specific domain/endpoint.\n2. **Service Identifier Resolution**:\n   Xray attaches the declared **Service Identifier (SID)** representing the exact capability or subsidiary service being invoked.\n3. **Stateless Delivery to Door `:8090`**:\n   Axum passes the Service Identifier directly into the gRPC door `:8090`. The door's interceptor checks the Service Identifier against the sealed capability catalog and routes directly to that service's handler.\n\n---\n\n### Proposed Steps to Prepare for the Post-12pm Identity Birth\n\nBefore touching any files or launching containers:\n\n1. **Define the Canonical Service Identifier**:\n   Assign the new subsidiary its official OP-DBUS Service Identifier (e.g. `mut.service.<name>.*@v1`).\n2. **Register the Service Identifier in the Identity Template**:\n   In `/srv/git/3tched-container/instances/chatbot-template.json`, set the container's environment so its local client identifies itself with this Service Identifier when dialing `:8090`.\n3. **Configure the Edge Route**:\n   Add the Service Identifier mapping to the edge gateway so incoming domain requests resolve directly to this service.\n\n---\n\n**Do you confirm this Service Identifier mapping before we prepare the container template for the new identity?**","thinking":"The phrase \"ser4vice identifier\" likely refers to \"Service Identifier\". Examining the subid grammar, the \"subject\" component clarifies the purpose, which in this context indicates an identifier related to a service. Analyzing telecommunications and edge telco architecture, this implies a service identifier is a key element.\n\n\nIn telco networks, a service identifier (SID) serves to classify traffic for policy and routing, consistent with 3GPP standards. The SID directs requests to backend service pipelines in edge gateways. Understanding this helps to map the user's \"SID\" to a technical definition.\n\n\n"}
