ions were verified using `ls -ld`.\r\ndocs/src/operations/network.md:45:- **Issuer works for that path:** router route selects `wgdecoy`, source `10.0.0.9`; issuer returns HTTP200, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://10.0.0.2:8080`, and an OIA1 document with a credential present and advertised door `https://10.0.0.2:8090`. No assertion/SID1/private key was logged or persisted.\r\ndocs/src/operations/network.md:54:- Owner explicitly chose restoring the existing human identity, not adopting the chatbot identity. OpenWrt `wgdecoy` now uses the saved human key, public key `0I5FNCuHAu62VctaNgOlJ7RgfejJpYe9Qd0VdPGesX8=`, alias `jeremy-wg-f036`, session `414fbc56-03fb-20ab-758a-bcc7a7cbdc0e`, principal `c9bdf32e-811d-2495-b688-277c9e5c4d36`. UCI and the live interface were updated. Decoy's old router peer was replaced with this key for `10.0.0.9/32` and persisted with `wg-quick save`.\r\n"}
